  "body": "PR #2216's sixteen-addition shear describes the F0/B1 boundary as a common data frame. The retained interface instead has `X_p: F` and `Y_p: F C_q^-1`. This package supplies exact counterexamples to applying its eight `Y_T -= X_A` updates as bare native scalars on arbitrary payloads. The paired bare updates also fail to conserve the logical selected sum on these inputs.\n\nFor a binary character with `q dot w = 1`, bare subtraction writes `-F chi_w`; the intended result is `-F C_q^-1 chi_w`. At target 21 (`q=289`, `w=1`), their physical values at address zero are `-i` and `-1`. The proof applies to every selected target and every positive tensor length, under the inherited boundary convention. The verifier binds all eight targets to the frozen packet and literal F0/B1 wrappers.\n\nThe contribution preserves #2216's reported rank-eight result on payload-constant inputs: all `C_q` act as identity there. It does not replay that group-algebra calculation. A typed adaptation or fusion with B1 may still implement the logical shear; this audit proves no extra-child lower bound and claims no supplier or new kappa. Its practical purpose is to prevent an unrestricted controller from inheriting the sixteen-addition invoice without a typed implementation.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Stored Z4 coefficient evaluation checks 4,096 character phases.\n- A separately implemented Gaussian-integer convolution checks eight explicit 512-entry physical vectors, including physical decoding of the nonzero sum change. It imports no predecessor executable.\n- Inverse-line adaptation passes; the positive-line sign and unadapted subtraction fail; constant-payload controls explain the original test's blind spot.\n- Direct optimized replay passes on CPython 3.15.0. The registered package replay passes on its required CPython 3.12.12 environment, an explicit compatibility exception. Metadata, source pins, and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nOne-command reproduction:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/qq16-shear-native-frame-audit/verify.py\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_QQ16_SHEAR_NATIVE_FRAME_AUDIT rejected_Y_adds=8 same_frame_X_updates=8 character_phases=4096 physical_vectors=8`.\n\nThe retained core boundary is inherited, not independently re-proved. This is not a full native traversal, hosting, or multiplication-theorem replay. No independent human review or formal-kernel proof is claimed. Base: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`; audited #2216 head: `b80e9ba43367fb8b20877a97da1cb677c34f9264`.\n\nCredit Ali Romman and the retained QQ16 lineage for the construction and reviews, and Cinna Davis for the proposed shear. Prepared for Charles Bethin with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. New material is Apache-2.0. The selected frontier and frozen predecessor files remain unchanged.\n",
